<title>MEXICO: Mexico sees record sugar harvest, exports up in 97.</title>
<headline>Mexico sees record sugar harvest, exports up in 97.</headline>
<dateline>CANCUN, Mexico 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico expects to export close to 600,000 tonnes of sugar in 1997 on top of a record 4.4-million-tonne harvest for the year, Commerce Minister Herminio Blanco said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect this year exports close to 600,000 tonnes,&quot; Blanco said at the inauguration of the F.O. Licht World Sugar and Sweeteners Conference in this Caribbean resort city.</p>
<p>Blanco said that in the last two years, Mexico exported a combined total of 670,000 tonnes of sugar. He said this year's record harvest would be a five percent increase over the previous crop.</p>
<p>((Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
